From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: fix IPQ5332 REO queue lookup register offsets

IPQ5332 supports REO queue reference lookup, but enabling the capability
alone is unsafe: its register table omits the queue address control and
maximum peer ID offsets. Their implicit zero values alias REO_GEN_ENABLE,
so LUT initialization overwrites the general enable register.

Populate both offsets to match Qualcomm's IPQ5332 register table in
wlan-ap. Keep the capability disabled: testing with WLAN.WBE.1.6-01270
still crashes the MLO partner even with correct register offsets.
This patch does not enable LUT setup or change firmware capabilities.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hal_qcn9274.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hal_qcn9274.c
@@ -430,6 +430,8 @@ const struct ath12k_hw_regs ipq5332_regs = {
 	.reo1_sw_cookie_cfg1 = 0x00000070,
 	.reo1_qdesc_lut_base0 = 0x00000074,
 	.reo1_qdesc_lut_base1 = 0x00000078,
+	.reo1_qdesc_addr = 0x0000007c,
+	.reo1_qdesc_max_peerid = 0x00000088,
 	.reo1_ring_base_lsb = 0x00000500,
 	.reo1_ring_base_msb = 0x00000504,
 	.reo1_ring_id = 0x00000508,
